2.4.m:
In place of both mother and father, a wise man should remember the guru alone;
what is not obtained through the guru is indeed not found anywhere else.
Through the guru's grace one attains everything; of this there is no doubt.
Medhāvī, Kapila, and Sumati of great austerity,
attained immortality through the proper service of their guru Gautama. / Therefore, with all effort, devoted to Viṣṇu in Kārtika,
one should perform service to the guru; therefrom one will attain liberation.
The best among twice-born who bestows Vaiṣṇava duty upon men,
attains the merit of giving the earth along with the oceans.
A cow fashioned of sesame, gold, silver, land, and clothing—
they shall make gifts of cows with wholehearted devotion, O you of good vows.
The gift of a maiden is superior to all gifts. / A thousand cows is equal to a hundred oxen;
a carriage is equal to ten oxen; a horse is equal to ten carriages;
the gift of an elephant is superior to thousands of gifts of horses;
and the gift of gold is equal to thousands of gifts of elephants;

One should wave the apāmārga and prapunnāḍa over one's head.
Having bathed, with wet clothes, one should offer a lamp to the two sons of Mṛtyu:
the two dogs, Śyāma and Śabala, brothers and servants of Yama;
the two sons of Mṛtyu are satisfied on the fourteenth by the gift of a lamp.
One should perform this ritual ablution together with loved ones and relatives;
having performed the water-offering belonging to the bath, one should then make a water-offering to Yama:
'To Yama, to the King of Dharma, to Death, and to the Ender;
to the son of Vivasvat, to Time, and to the Destroyer of all beings;
to Audumbara, to Dadhna, to the Dark, to the Supreme Lord;
to Vṛkodara, to Citra, to Citragupta—homage to you!'
These should be the fourteen mantras, each accompanied by 'namas';
with each one, one should offer three palmfuls of water mixed with sesame seeds.
It may be performed with the sacred thread over the left shoulder or over the right shoulder;
for Yama possesses a two-fold nature: both godhead and ancestorhood.
Even one whose father is living should perform the water-offering to Yama and Bhīṣma;
